    "originalInstructions": "1. Order a leg of mutton boned.\n2. Wipe, stuff, sew, and place in deep pan.\n3. Cook five minutes in one-fourth cup butter, a slice each of onion, carrot, and turnip cut in dice, one-half bay leaf, and a sprig each of thyme and parsley.\n4. Add three cups hot water, one and one-half teaspoons salt, and twelve peppercorns; pour over mutton.\n5. Cover closely, and cook slowly three hours, uncovering for the last half-hour.\n6. Remove from pan to hot platter.\n7. Brown three tablespoons butter, add four tablespoons flour, and stir until well browned; then pour on slowly the strained liquor; there should be one and three-fourths cups.",
